702 0 obj
<</Title(Insight  Surprisingly, most of the products in this list \(14 out of 20\) have exactly the same price: $903. This looks strange because they are very different items, like socks, sports bras, and jackets. Maybe it is a data error, so I would check these products first.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 665 0 R/Prev 739 0 R>>
endobj

703 0 obj
<</Title(order_type)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 666 0 R/Next 740 0 R>>
endobj

704 0 obj
<</Title(Insight  First orders bring nearly 64% of sales \(80,131 orders, $6.9M\) and repeat orders 36% \($3.9M\). Average order value is almost identical \($86.26 vs $86.93\), so repeat customers do not spend more per order. They just come back, about 0.56 repeat orders per customer. Winning new customers matters most, and bundles or loyalty offers could lift repeat baskets.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 666 0 R/Prev 741 0 R>>
endobj

705 0 obj
<</Title(count)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 606 0 R/Prev 667 0 R/Next 742 0 R>>
endobj

706 0 obj
<</Title(The Analysis :  Returned orders are grouped by product category. The return rate is the value of returned items divided by the category\220s total sales. Data comes from order_items, joined with orders for status and products for category.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 606 0 R/Prev 743 0 R/Next 668 0 R>>
endobj

